rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T22:48:08-07:00","id":1488535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1487305-bizarre-combinations-of-seeming-and-kith?p=1488527#post1488527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's Mergo's Wetnurse? Darkling Playmate or Chatelaine that hasn't escaped Durance yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Keeper\u2019s Title, considering the lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T08:24:05-07:00","id":1488825,"title":"","content":"A Draconic Grimm. Sewn into a book of fables, she was forced to quest endlessly against the same dragon, on loop. If the story was ever changed, even in the slightest, she\u2019d suffer. Now free, she will make her OWN story on her terms.<br /> <br /> An Incubus Ogre. The Endlessly Walking Lion wanted a mate, so he took one from one of the city\u2019s homeless youth, and turned him into a lion <i>almost</i> as magnetizing and attractive as himself.<br /> <br /> A Levinquick Wizened. He was electrician in a robot city. He was given impossible tasks and told to fix them, ASAP!, or else. He eventually sabotaged the city\u2019s outer perimeter to make an escape, but a portion of Arcadian electricity traveled out Ironside with him.<br /> <br /> A Sandharrowed Fairest. She was made to dance for the Grim Dragon, but, when her dancing failed to instill passion in him, he unleashed fiery breath, burning her to ash. The next morning she\u2019d reconstitute herself, and the cycle would begin again.<br /> <br /> A Shadowsoul Ogre.<br /> <br /> A Troll Fairest. The Stag King needed an enforcer, but he could not tolerate hideousness. So, he took this woman and made her into his Game Warden. She had to play a careful game of subterfuge and countermeasure with the other Game Wardens the Stag King over the years...<br /> <br /> A Tunnelgrub Fairest. Surrounded by hideous brutes, this changeling, a \u2018son\u2019 of the King Under the Mountain, was forbidden to see anything beautiful, not his own reflection or the sun. He grew pale and his heart died. Even back on Earth, his emotions are moody and he shuns the day.<br /> <br /> A Windwing Wizened. The Lab, full of faceless scientists, always needed new animal test subjects for its irrelevant line of cosmetics. That these were once human made the tests that much more applicable, or so the scientists said. They endured hell, until a frantic little bat escaped her cage, fled through ventilation duct Hedge and back into Earthly reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 11-09-2022, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T13:00:59-07:00","id":1488871,"title":"","content":"This is why I love the Changeling The Lost series so much. The storytelling ideas are endless for the True Fae and what kind of durance you can have for a Lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":".  Fixing careless mistakes in the post 08-03-2022, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T13:45:42-07:00","id":1488876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1487305-bizarre-combinations-of-seeming-and-kith?p=1488871#post1488871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why I love the Changeling The Lost series so much. The storytelling ideas are endless for the True Fae and what kind of durance you can for a Lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed! This is an aspect of the game I as well enjoy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T16:19:15-07:00","id":1488899,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s some more:<br /> <br /> An Airtouched Wizened. The wind must blow! The breeze must soar! The Butterfly Queen would die if she touched the earth, so she kidnapped this poor meteorologist and turned him into an updraft, to keep his monarch aloft. When he failed...as he <i>always</i> did\u2014-he\u2019d turned into a vacuum to scream silently.<br /> <br /> An Antiquarian Beast. This little turtle, once a blind man who made a foolish bargain in order to see again, scribbles information down on <i>everywhere</i>, much to the pleasure Who Bookbinds With Blood, this changeling\u2019s Keeper. Escaping Arcadia has not changed this mania even in the slightest.<br /> <br /> A Draconic Ogre. The Queen Adorned in Gold is rich, <i>fabulously</i> rich, but thieveswere everywhere. (That some were her own changelings ordered to rob from her meant nothing. It was an irrelevancy.) So, she got herself a dragon, taking from a burn ward victim\u2019s shattered body.<br /> <br /> A Farwalker Grimm. Not sure, yet.<br /> <br /> A Flowering Wizened. He was a bonsai. Once,he was a man. He studied botany and practiced flower-arrangement as a hobby. Now, the Mute Gardener pruned him each day, an agony that never ended, until he finally <i>escaped</i> Ironside.<br /> <br /> A Gargantuan Wizened. Tested in a military-based Lab full of nameless, faceless scientist Wisps, this poor fellow had subdermal expandable armor implanted under his skin. At whim, he could transform into a war mech, but each transformation either way was an unbearable agony. Eventually, he ditched his weaponry and ran Ironside.<br /> <br /> A Helldiver Grimm. She was a folklorist and Wiccan, and <i>willingly</i> allowed the Mad Tale-Teller to escort her off to Arcadia. There, transformed into a tome containing a summoning ritual, she was sent into the Hedge to lure unwary mortals to perform the spell, whereupon they\u2019re whisked away to be the property of the Mad Tale-Teller.<br /> <br /> A Runnerswift Darkling. The Hunter of the Perfect Rose loves to hunt, and this hind, once a Track-and-Field rising star, has evaded the Hunter the longest. So clever was she she found her way back Ironside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 08-13-2022, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T16:50:18-07:00","id":1489591,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s some more:<br /> <br /> An Airtouched Darkling.<br /> <br /> A Chimeric Elemental. Everyone calls him Fusion, which aggravates him, but it is appropriate, for, in his durance, he was made into a cold fusion reactor powering a robot city. Remembering his mortal life he pulled his plutonium rods out of the coolant, then wrenched himself free and ran Ironside while the robot city went into panic-mode.<br /> <br /> A Flowering Ogre. The Primeval Forest, a Title for a Gentry that manifested as, you guessed it, a forest, took a dozen mortals and planted them in a circle in the clearing. One was made into a redwood tree. Even escaping Ironside, he remained gargantuan in size, skin made of wood...<br /> <br /> A Gargantuan Beast.<br /> <br /> A Leechfingers Ogre. The Chiropteran Cage was a Title that manifested as a great, infinitely large yet utterly cramped bird cage. There, inside itself, it kept birds, bats, insects and more, all of them winged. This Ogre became a bat.<br /> <br /> A Riddleseeker Ogre. He was made into a minotaur in a trap-ladened labyrinth, the plaything of the Ever-Victorious Hero. He grew strong as traps kept catching him, but, in time, he became cleverer and cleverer as he experienced each new permutation of a trap.<br /> <br /> A Snowskin Wizened. In the Lab, faceless Wisp scientists conducted experiments in cryogenics. This old man thought he\u2019d signed up for something very different... He was put in deep freeze and thawed again and again, til the cryogenic freeze became part of who he was.<br /> <br /> A Stonebones Grimm.<br /> <br /> A Woodblood Beast. He is perhaps the changeling held longest in Arcadian captivity, a state of being he still endures. A vast sea turtle with trees and grass growing on his back, he has been lost in the Sea Storm Eternal since the end of the American Civil War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 11-09-2022, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T19:13:08-07:00","id":1489702,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s some more.<br /> <br /> A Bloodbrute Fairest. The Ever-Victorious Hero loved having beautiful changelings fight to the death for his amusement. This violence became part of them, and they\u2019re just as deadly as they are attractive.<br /> <br /> A Corpsegrinder Wizened. In the Year of the Plague, some changelings were faced with starvation. Some died, but others adapted, eating carrion. Slowly, they became rats, but were set ablaze every time the cycle reset. This brave little rat, burnt beyond recognition, escapes Ironside.<br /> <br /> A Fireheart Beast. The Hunter of the Perfect Rose loved falconry, but no ordinary bird would suffice. He captured this poor woman and allowed a phoenix Wisp to devour her. The Wisp then laid an egg, and a new phoenix, once human, emerged from the shell.<br /> <br /> A Gargantuan Grimm. He had to write a book in a single night, or else the Merciless Abbot would put him through horrifying ordeals. Again and again he failed, and each attempted book was destroyed in the monastery\u2019s crematoria. Eventually, the author fell upon the secret of it, and wove <i>himself</i> into the book, creating a massive tome that told the man\u2019s story from start to finish, leaving out. Impressed, the Merciless Abbot <i>let him go</i>?<br /> <br /> A Gravewight Elemental. A surgeon was taken by the Hunter of the Perfect Rose, then buried under the earth almost immediately. Slowly, he spread himself thin, the surgeon did, and was then used by the Hunter as a graveyard for past hunts. Eventually, the surgeon remembered who he was, vomited up all the Hedge ghosts slumbering within himself and made a run for it.<br /> <br /> A Larcenist Elemental. Swept up after wishes he could fantastical adventures, this had his hands and feet chopped off and replaced with mercury prosthetics. He would burgle the houses of the Rakshasa\u2019s fellow Gentry, using his hands to become whatever lock he needed at that moment.<br /> <br /> A Lurkglider Wizened. The Queen of Hell, a True Fae obsessed with Western depictions of demons, sometimes kidnap mortals to turn them into replicas or such things. This poor boy became an imp.<br /> <br /> A Nightsinger Ogre. The Hag made a mortal man into a stone idol of some nameless pagan god, with a hole straight through his head where he mouth should be. The wind blew through him, and he howled. Over time, he learned to modulate his pitch. Even now, in Ironside, his stone body belies his angelic singing.<br /> <br /> An Oracle Elemental. The Ever-Seeing Eye, a gigantic Gentry that fills the entire sky of its Arcadian Realm, wishes to behold all things at once. This poor woman, once quite elderly, was transformed into a prop for divination\u2014-a crystal ball. Eventually, her powers allowed her to remember her past and go Ironside.<br /> <br /> A Roteater Elemental. The Architect of Blurred Dreams needed fungi to break down the ample rot and carrion his experiments inevitably left behind, so, this stoner was given a new kind of high. Even after escape, the scent of carrion gets his mouth watering, and bright lights are painful to endure!<br /> <br /> A Roteater Fairest. Known as \u2018black angels\u2019, these Fairest are the beautiful, obsidian, white haired heralds of the Hag, and feast on the flesh of the fallen.<br /> <br /> A Skitterskulk Fairest. She\u2019s the queen, and the hive loved her. But the Great Egg couldn\u2019t hatch, and vented its fury on its adopted mother. Eventually, the queen deserted the hive, and found her way Ironside.<br /> <br /> A Steepscrambler Elemental. An infinitely tall chimney needed a fire to light it up. A poor boy from Ironside was turned into chimney fire and smoke, til he escaped through the opening at the top.<br /> <br /> A Windwing Fairest. The Butterfly Queen demands her paramours be able to flit about with her, so, the men she takes have Arcadian butterflies of enormous size implanted into their backs, following the spinal cord. Over time, symbionts and host become one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 11-14-2022, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T18:13:08-07:00","id":1489982,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s some more.<br /> <br /> An Antiquarian Ogre. Bloated but obese, every inch of this gargantuan changeling, even folds in the flesh hidden by blubber, is covered in newspaper print, from all over Ironside. <br /> <br /> A Brewer Elemental. The Hall of Alcoholic History is an Arcadian Realm where the party never stopped, where rest was impossible, where happiness was mandatory and horrible things happened just out of the revelers\u2019 sight. This poor man was one of several living refreshments, in his case, cider. When he burst from his keg and made a run for it, the other revelers cheered him on...<br /> <br /> A Daitya Beast. Mommy was sometimes worried about intruders, so she made a guard dog from a man who <i>hated</i> dogs. Trained brutally to attack and devour anything that remotely threatened Mommy, this changeling made his escape as Mommy dealt with a Larcenist sent by a rival Gentry.<br /> <br /> A Di-Cang Beast. He was the Sacred Bull, taken from a mundane life to serve the Stag King. The Sacred Bull\u2019s blood healed wounded forest creatures, and his tears raised the dead. But, on the most blisteringly hot day of Summer, the Sacred Bull was sacrificed to something old, nameless and evil. Even after escaping Ironside the Sacred Bull finds it difficult to turn away those in need.<br /> <br /> A Di-Cang Wizened. The Merciless Abbot had an apothecary to tend to monks and nuns who failed to show sufficient piety, but this apothecary was punished for even the least mistake in her brewing of salves, elixirs and draughts.<br /> <br /> A Drudge Beast. Ironside, he was a brutal taskmaster in his office, running his interns ragged. Then, the Man in the Black Suit came and took the office manager away. Put on a farm the Man in the Black Suit owned, he became a literal workhorse. Even after his escape, this changeling never shirks hard work.<br /> <br /> A Drudge Fairest. To the machine lord Wisps that ruled the robot city, only the very best technology would suffice. Even worker-drones had to be perfect, and sometimes, perfection meant beauty. This woman, a robot so perfectly human it appeared alive, was just such a worker-drone.<br /> <br /> A Fireheart Darkling. This fire burns, but dimly. An ember that refuses to go out, he escaped a Gentry named Heart of the Ocean, who used him as a lamp aboard the Other\u2019s galleon. He\u2019s a bitter, sour, but dependable member of the Day Court!<br /> <br /> A Gandharva Elemental. Our Father Who Art in the City, modeling himself after the greatest propagandists Ironside, took this radio DJ and turned him into a propaganda piece aired 24/7 on the City\u2019s only radio channel. Every now and again, another propaganda piece would be broadcast. The message was simple: <i>Obey your leader. Your leader is divine. Give yourself over to the leader.</i> Somehow, this particular radio broadcast, made to appeal to anyone, found a signal leading to Earth. He took it.<br /> <br /> A Goblin Ogre. In the court of the Glacial Giant King, some giants were larger than others. This particular Ogre, was still towering over most changelings, was a rat scurrying underfoot to his betters. Put to work in cavernous duct systems too small for other giants, this Goblin Ogre learned a great many things, and used that knowledge to go back Ironside.<br /> <br /> A Pishacha Beast. Is it male? Is it female? It no longer remembers. Resembling a giant diseased rat, this changeling was used by Obese Abyss to clean up her dishes after they were eaten. It\u2019s sanity shattered under the weight of the horrifying....<i>material</i>...it was forced to devour.<br /> <br /> A Sandharrowed Ogre.<br /> <br /> A Skogsra Wizened. A Game Warden of the Stag King, this poor woman could simply never do her job <i>right</i>. Her punishments were many and varied, and finally, unable to live like that any longer, she escaped to Earth.<br /> <br /> A Smith Fairest. Sometimes, the Brute desires a paramour, but blacksmithing is inextricably linked to his nature, and is inescapable even here. She was captured and brought to Arcadia to work the Brute\u2019s forge.<br /> <br /> A Stonebones Fairest. Made of living marble, he was taken by the Ever-Victorious Hero and turned into a \u2018pretty thing\u2019 chained to the Gentry\u2019s throne. He hasn\u2019t spoken since his escape; the freehold worries for his Clarity...<br /> <br /> A Thusser Beast. After a successful hunt, the Hunter of the Perfect Rose desired a choir of songbirds sing for him. This poor lad was one such songbird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 11-19-2022, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T11:31:27-07:00","id":1490041,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s some more.<br /> <br /> An Ask-wee-da-eed Ogre. The Great Hero Yi shot down nine suns, but it was the Monkey King who caught one as it fell and kept it as a pet. As the sun died, it whispered to him the secret of making more. All it would take ways an honorable man, and an incantation to ignite him. Thus, down the millennia, the Monkey King has had nine suns in his sky, hidden from the rest of Heaven.<br /> <br /> A Cleareyes Elemental. Found on Deep Space Station #35, a man who was once an astronomer became an insanely advanced telescope, that the other captive changelings on the station might oooh and aaaah at the majesty of Apollo Alpha, a Gentry which shaped itself into an entire galaxy. Even after escaping, this changeling\u2019s eyesight remains extremely clean.<br /> <br /> A Coldscale Grimm. The Hag turned this poor man into a snake, then skinned him. Too afraid to die, his soul clung to its skin. Upon this skin the Hag wrote spells and Contracts and used him as part of her strange grimoire. Eventually, he regained the will to move, and slithered to his escape.<br /> <br /> A Cyclops Fairest. The Eternal Princess must have her gallant knight, and this man fulfilled that role before he went Ironside. Wounded in a joust, he\u2019s only one good eye left, but constant jousting made him incredibly strong.<br /> <br /> A Di-Cang Ogre.<br /> <br /> A Flamesiren Beast. Caught in eternal darkness streaked with neon glowing colors allowing some degree of sight, this young man resembles an obsidian wolf covered in mass amounts of fiery glowing neon red tattoos. Other creatures followed him, but the King of Colors could never stand competition. After a time, this changeling fled and his Arcadian adherents were massacred.<br /> <br /> An Illes Fairest. Prom was coming up! (Prom is <i>always</i> coming up!) The \u2018students\u2019 must wear their best, for the Prom Queen will tolerate nothing less. This girl, snatched on the night of her mundane prom, was turned into a hideous hag, then given enchanted clothing that made her more beautiful than any other \u2018student\u2019. At midnight, the Prom Queen would unmask this poor girl and everyone would make fun of her. But, hey! Prom\u2019s coming up! Maybe next time will be better.<br /> <br /> A Moonborn Elemental. The idol of the Mother of the Moon screamed silently as atrocities disguised as shamanic rites took place before her frozen eyes each night. Eventually, the idol could bear no more, and made a mad daytime escape Ironside, while the Mother of the Moon slept beneath the earth.<br /> <br /> An Oni Beast. Mommy had <i>very specific rules</i> visitors to her estate <i>must</i> obey. This man became a snarling hound that was set loose on rules-breakers. Even now, having escaped Ironside, this changeling can\u2019t abide those who lie or cheat.<br /> <br /> An Oracle Ogre. The Hag sometimes needed assistance in her witchery, and this poor woman, once a Wiccan author, was transformed into a lesser hag. She divines for her mistress, and fears whenever he prophecies go wrong...as they inevitably eventually will.<br /> <br /> A Telluric Beast. Caught in eternal darkness streaked with neon glowing colors allowing some degree of sight, this poor man, once a budding fashion icon, was made into a hunter. If he he ate a hundred other changelings, he\u2019d be free. A sleek, cat-like Beast with rainbow neon glowing colors, he is now a Loyalist on Earth.<br /> <br /> A Treasured Beast. A red minotaur adorned with unremovable and copious gold ornaments, he was kept as a showpiece by the Ever-Victorious Hero. Even after escaping, this changeling is obsessed with accumulating as much wealth as he possibly can.<br /> <br /> A Treasured Darkling.<br /> <br /> A Tunnelgrub Ogre. Sometimes a giant displeased the Glacial Giant King, so he would exile these changelings into the tunnels beneath his palace, to fend for themselves. Of course, he never bothers to tell them of gigantic rat hobs that hunt by scent in the freezing dark...<br /> <br /> A Weisse Frau Darkling. She was made into a spider, but escaped her first Keeper, only to end up on the Arcadian farm of the Man in the Black Suit. She was horrified, as pigs were led to slaughter, so, she wove words into her webs, to dazzle and amaze. But she couldn\u2019t save them all, and, one stormy night, was flushed down drainpipe Henge back Ironside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 11-09-2022, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T06:55:12-07:00","id":1490131,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s some more.<br /> <br /> An Airtouched Ogre. The Sea Storm Eternal raged forever, venting its fury even on itself. This man, a sea-faring explorer, was caught up in an unnatural wind and transformed into a hurricane, to rage along with his Keeper. Even after escaping, this changeling\u2019s fury knows no end.<br /> <br /> An Ask-wee-da-eed Beast. In the black abyss of the Sea Storm Eternal, all who survived swam as bizarre, alien fish in the darkness. This woman was no different, and became an anglerfish to survive. She saw many wonders and horrors in the deeps, before she found a grotto that led back to Ironside shore. Now, strange and powerful fish-hobs able to assume human form court her her with fine gifts.<br /> <br /> A Larcenist Beast. She was a homeless youth, once, before she was taken away by the Primeval Forest. Denied food, denied water, denied shelter, she had to steal just to survive, until finally she became the forest\u2019s greatest thief\u2014-a raccoon. Even after escaping to Earth, she has a phobia of starvation.<br /> <br /> A Di-Cang Darkling. In the Arcadian nuclear wasteland just beyond the robot city, mutants, the war\u2019s only survivors, only kept surviving because of the Survey Corps. Wearing an environment suit with no flesh showing anywhere, Survey Corps doctors became interchangeable.<br /> <br /> A Drudge Darkling. The Master of the Manor demanded his lowest house staff remain unseen\u2014-even being spotted by another changeling was enough to encourage hideous punishments. BUT, they still must complete their tasks on time. This changeling figured out how to do both.<br /> <br /> A Lurkglider Beast. The Hunter of the Perfect Rose turned this man into a manticore, then set him loose. The manticore would be killed then resurrected to be hunted all over again. Eventually, the manticore made a successful bid for freedom!<br /> <br /> A Moonborn Wizened. He\u2019d done it! He\u2019d joined the Fraternal Hermetic Order of the Golden Dawning of a New Age For the Betterment of All Mankind (aka, FHOGDNAFBAM, for short). At last he\u2019d learnt genuine occult truths! The Wizard demanded this man perform the lunar rites, but no matter how he tried, proper enunciation eluded him. The rituals were simply too complex. The Wizard would lock this changeling into the Box of Deletrious Agony and Uncountable Sigils of Pain For the Unworthy (aka, the BDAUSPFU, for short). But he could never learn the rites properly. Escaping Ironside, he is an obsessive student of Contracts and all things of the Wyrd.<br /> <br /> A Muse Ogre. A titan of living sound and congealed noise, Our Father Who Art in the City is propaganda, personified. He broadcasts through all media to the captive changelings in his city-Realm, delighting as their wills collapse, the urge to resist slowly dying inside them. This Ogre was transformed into a biomechanical antenna array, much akin to the creepypasta character Sirenhead.<br /> <br /> A Palewraith Wizened. If she was spotted, the ghostling was dragged with iron hooks into the cellar, where hot bronze knives awaited. So, to this avoid this punishment, she figured out how to <i>cease to exist</i>.<br /> <br /> A Polychromatic Beast. Caught in eternal darkness streaked with neon glowing colors allowing some degree of sight, this lonely young woman was transformed into an obsidian owl covered in glowing lines of neon purple, and hunted with cruel abandon. Even after escaping, her low Clarity score is quite indicative of her unquenchable need to hurt people...<br /> <br /> A Soldier Beast. Used as a literal warhorse in the never-ending Arcadian campaign of the Tireless General, this changeling fled when his unit routed, and galloped like mad all the way back to Earth. Even now, he isn\u2019t afraid of a fight.<br /> <br /> A Water-Born Fairest. A mermaid. What <i>else</i> could she be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 11-10-2022, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T09:58:03-07:00","id":1490143,"title":"","content":"You have some great ideas for your Changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T11:18:31-07:00","id":1490156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1487305-bizarre-combinations-of-seeming-and-kith?p=1490143#post1490143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have some great ideas for your Changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I\u2019m less skilled with game mechanics, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T11:40:15-07:00","id":1490413,"title":"","content":"Here is a couple of ideas from me.<br /> <br /> A Hunterheat Draconic. A elegant looking predator that can lull you with it's beauty and then strikes to take you down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T18:41:50-07:00","id":1491149,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s some more.<br /> <br /> A Blightbent Beast. The Architect of Blurred Dreams needs test subjects to experiment his concoctions upon, and this poor boy, literally made into a guinea pig, was one such test subject. Mutated and twisted and toxic after years of torture, the guinea pig escaped, now a walking nightmare.<br /> <br /> A Draconic Darkling. An escaped concubine of the Endlessly Walking Lion, this Obsidian-colored Sphinx feels compelled to make every word he speaks a lie.<br /> <br /> A Levinbolt Fairest. The Sea Storm Eternal needs captains for skyfaring pirate fleets. This woman was one such thief of thunder, and, even after escaping, she retains the Lightning still.<br /> <br /> A Levinbolt Ogre. A Lab full of grim, faceless scientist-Whisps made this woman into a hulking cyborg with a taser in her left arm. She escaped, and cannot yet found a way to undo her cybernetic transformation.<br /> <br /> A Playmate Darkling.<br /> <br /> A Polychromatic Ogre.<br /> <br /> A Polychromatic Wizened.<br /> <br /> A Sandharrowed Wizened. The Curious Painter needed mummies to use as painting-material. (Note: Yes, this was actually a thing one point in the real world.) But only the best materials would do. This man, seized Ironside, was embalmed and buried in the sand. Too bad the Curious Painted forgot about his impromptu mummy...<br /> <br /> A Skogsra Ogre. Many half-imaginary horrors wander the psychosis-inducing Arcadian Realm of the Architect of Blurred Dreams, and this fungal hulk was charged with keeping them hemmed in. Even after escaping, his abysmally low Clarity ensures he\u2019s never certain what\u2019s real and what\u2019s not.<br /> <br /> A Smith Elemental. <i>Bend and burn and break and mend./Heat, reshape, reforge, make clean./Wash away the iron cold, then retreat, reshape, remold./Anvil strong, anvil hot, iron breaks, the anvil does not.</i><br /> <br /> A Steepscrambler Fairest. He is dead, or so he fervently believes. Sculpted from ivory, he hangs precariously on the Pillar of Naraka, the living world high above. He <i>must</i> keep climbing, he <i>must</i>...!<br /> <br /> A Witchtooth Beast. The Covey, a trio of Wisp-Title Gentry, need animals to sacrifice to the Mad Arcadian moon, and only the finest animals sufficed. This man, taken and fed like a pig til he became one, slipped his cage the night his entrails were to be read! He remembers their magics, and now has magic of his own!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 11-14-2022, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T14:28:57-08:00","id":1496542,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s some more...<br /> <br /> A Bloodbrute Beast. Under her Mask she\u2019s a humanoid boar, angry and full of hate. The Man in the Black Suit held her on his farm. Upon escape, her rage dimmed somewhat upon meeting a surprisingly gentle MMA fighter named Axel. He\u2019s training her now to enter the ring herself, and the love she feels for him cools the volcanic rage inside her.<br /> <br /> A Gravewight Beast. In the Collapsed Spiral, a claustrophobic subterranean labyrinth, dead things clung tenaciously to a life that has rejected them. Here, in the lightless depths, naturally mummified animal corpses, remade from human captives, sink into wet earth and slowly fossilize, becoming the Still Court of the Starving Wolf. Every so often, though, an undead man-turned-animal remembers what it is to breathe, and makes a run for it.<br /> <br /> An Incubus Beast. A musky, primeval satyr, this changeling was meant to be a concubine of the Queen Inside the Tree, but escaped Ironside. He\u2019s a musician, and is quite the bed-hopper.<br /> <br /> A Manikin Beast. In the Court of the Moon King, during the mortal Renaissance, Gentry we\u2019re fascinated by the primitive automata of the time, and a flurry of such changelings were produced. This mechanical lion, a favorite \u2018pet\u2019 of the Moon King, never escaped Arcadia and now has completely forgotten his life Ironside. Escape, for him, is now impossible...<br /> <br /> A Blightbent Darkling. Turned into a giant moth feasting on the secretions of the Architect of Blurred Dreams, upon escaping Ironside, she turned self-made drug kingpin.<br /> <br /> A Corpsegrinder Darkling. Blind, with milked over eyes, patchy fur and chipped hooves, this goat-man scavenged from the corpses produced each year by the Year of Plague. He loves the taste of disease-ridden human flesh, the more putrid, the better. Having escaped Ironside, he supports himself by working as a mob hitman. Ghosts flit near him, in Twilight.<br /> <br /> A Manikin Darkling. Appearing as a Southeast Asian Shadow-puppet, he is a feared member of the Thai Tiger Court, a Court focused around subtle manipulation. He has a great many Goblin Contracts, which gets him <i>into</i> trouble as often as it gets him <i>out</i> of trouble.<br /> <br /> A Gravewight Elemental. The gravesite of the Lord Under The Hill required a suitable tombstone that mourners might make eternal grief before; this man, a former heavyweight MMA fighter, made for suitable materials. Even after he escaped, he remains physically slow but powerful and mentally caustic if honest.<br /> <br /> A Windwing Fairest. The Queen of Hell, a Gentry obsessed with medieval Christian depictions of Hell, turns her captive changelings into devilish forms. Except, <i>this</i> time, Her Infernal Majesty wanted an <i>angel</i>...<br /> <br /> A Gravewight Fairest. The Covey, a trio of hag-Wisps, celebrate the turning of the seasons with the Gilded Prince, a castrated eunuch, flesh rent and riven, clad in gold and scented beautifully. He whispers auguries to the Covey, but, every winter solstice, the Gilded Prince is sacrificed, to ensure the return of Arcadian Spring, and a new one must be found to replace him.<br /> <br /> A Gravewight Grimm. Under her Mask a dessicated undead horror, every inch of this leathery creature is marked by the Enochian script invented by Dr. John Dee. Revealing nonsensical prophecies that foretell contradictory events, this changeling escaped a Gentry called Who Bookbinds in Blood.<br /> <br /> A Polychromatic Grimm.<br /> <br /> A Cleareyes Ogre.<br /> <br /> A Gravewight Ogre. The Keeper called Apollo Alpha needs aliens, and the only way he\u2019ll find them is by kidnapping humans and changing them to fit the bill. Locked inside a coffin straight from the artwork of HR Giger in a planet-Realm of chthonic, ancient prehuman civilizations, this hulking xeno-horror was once a construction worker with astronomy as an avid hobby. Locked in crysostasis, should he waken, he will be a terrifying monstrosiry to those unlucky enough to encounter him.<br /> <br /> A Gravewight Wizened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 11-11-2022, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T18:38:25-08:00","id":1496670,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s some more.<br /> <br /> An Ask-wee-de-end Darkling.<br /> <br /> A Broadback Elemental.<br /> <br /> A Broadback Grimm. A pallid mendicant carrying a massive book of hidden oracles chained onto his back, this changeling is a Roman Catholic priest, albeit of a <i>very</i> borderline-heretical beliefs. The Merciless Abbot, his Keeper, avidly wishes to recapture the mendicant.<br /> <br /> A Cleareyes Fairest. She was a bird, but her wings clipped, kept as a pet by the Merciless Abbot. She\u2019d see into the hearts of others, but saw only terror, never treachery. Eventually, she had enough, and fled Ironside.<br /> <br /> A Coldscale Darkling.<br /> <br /> A Coldscale Elemental.<br /> <br /> A Dancer Beast. A super-slender and ultra-flexible \u2018hybrid-form werewolf\u2019, she was the prized pet of the Hunter of the Perfect Rose. After escaping Ironside, she took up a job at a local community theater. A Predator King Werewolf has been eyeballing her, lately.<br /> <br /> A Draconic Ogre. The Carp King swam mindlessly, an aquatic behemoth, and would lure Ironside swimmers to it by mimicking the cries of people in pain. Those it kidnapped had no choice but to become enormous carp, themselves, equally mindless.<br /> <br /> An Oni Fairest.<br /> <br /> A Skitterskulk Ogre.<br /> <br /> A Thusser Darkling.<br /> <br /> A Water-Born Darkling.<br /> <br /> A Water-Born Ogre. The Covey would sometimes take apprentices, mortal women who would be painfully transformed into looming swamp hags, to tend sacred sites throughout the Covey\u2019s Realm. This woman escaped, but can\u2019t enter a swamp without suffering nightmares of her durance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 11-19-2022, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-12T09:54:46-08:00","id":1496919,"title":"","content":"I wonder what a Coldscale Darkling would look like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-12T12:38:41-08:00","id":1496931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1487305-bizarre-combinations-of-seeming-and-kith?p=1496919#post1496919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder what a Coldscale Darkling would look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>A deep sea fish, maybe? A black snake? An archeopterix?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-14T07:18:28-08:00","id":1497091,"title":"","content":"Fairest Hunterheart -- Princess Twilight Sparkle of The Rainbow Brigade<br /> <br /> The Crystal Kingdom was a utopia that had lasted for a thousand years, ruled by Her Benevolent Eminence, The Kaleidoscope Queen. And defenders of the realm, The Knights of The Rainbow Brigade, were her hand-picked guardians of Truth, Love, and Happiness. Together they rode forth on their Apocalypse Ponies to banish The False, reclaim Those Who Wandered, and who enforced The Decree of Joy, the edict stating that the citizens of The Crystal Kingdom should know nothing but contentment and love and bliss. Her Beloved Eminence scoured the world for the best, the prettiest, the most capable children to knight, sweeping them away from their miserable mortal lives to a realm of wonders and protect their happy, shiny, perfect world.<br /> <br /> The Crystal Kingdom was a horrible, bright lie, ruled by an autocratic Gentry who snatched children with promises they could be pretty magical princesses, decked them out with Hedgespun livery, gifted them with Token weapons and monstrous, hellfire-breathing steeds, taught them magic to sear the flesh and paint smiles on people's souls, then made them police her Goblin subjects, destroying dissidents and capturing those who tried to flee. She instilled a deep paranoia in each of her Knightss that they had to watch their fellows for any sign of unhappiness or disloyalty, and gaslight them relentlessly to quash their doubts and growing PTSD. Those who broke were set on by their peers.<br /> <br /> But one got away...<br /> <br /> ((Why yes, I <i>have</i> been reading through Princess: The Hopeful, why do you ask?))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-14T08:41:20-08:00","id":1497093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1487305-bizarre-combinations-of-seeming-and-kith?p=1497091#post1497091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fairest Hunterheart -- Princess Twilight Sparkle of The Rainbow Brigade<br /> <br /> The Crystal Kingdom was a utopia that had lasted for a thousand years, ruled by Her Benevolent Eminence, The Kaleidoscope Queen. And defenders of the realm, The Knights of The Rainbow Brigade, were her hand-picked guardians of Truth, Love, and Happiness. Together they rode forth on their Apocalypse Ponies to banish The False, reclaim Those Who Wandered, and who enforced The Decree of Joy, the edict stating that the citizens of The Crystal Kingdom should know nothing but contentment and love and bliss. Her Beloved Eminence scoured the world for the best, the prettiest, the most capable children to knight, sweeping them away from their miserable mortal lives to a realm of wonders and protect their happy, shiny, perfect world.<br /> <br /> The Crystal Kingdom was a horrible, bright lie, ruled by an autocratic Gentry who snatched children with promises they could be pretty magical princesses, decked them out with Hedgespun livery, gifted them with Token weapons and monstrous, hellfire-breathing steeds, taught them magic to sear the flesh and paint smiles on people's souls, then made them police her Goblin subjects, destroying dissidents and capturing those who tried to flee. She instilled a deep paranoia in each of her Knightss that they had to watch their fellows for any sign of unhappiness or disloyalty, and gaslight them relentlessly to quash their doubts and growing PTSD. Those who broke were set on by their peers.<br /> <br /> But one got away...<br /> <br /> ((Why yes, I <i>have</i> been reading through Princess: The Hopeful, why do you ask?))</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Finally</i>! THANK YOU for contributing! I thought Lysander was the only one who would!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-14T13:49:39-08:00","id":1497116,"title":"","content":"It helps that I had the character concept first, then when I was looking for Seeming/Kith combinations I realized I'd come up with one that would fit with this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-14T14:11:14-08:00","id":1497119,"title":"","content":"To be blunt, it can be hard to come up with salient, meaningful concepts based purely on Kith/Seeming combos. Maybe post a few at a time as you finish them, and people will follow suit?","signature":"<hr class